Subject: [sshmap fork 0011] OSC 8 hyperlinks — the link a program sends rides the CELL

Provenance: sshmap (v1.9, ROADMAP task 1) — the terminal-link ask. The vendored 0.8.2 dispatches OSC
            `0`/`1`/`2` only (the `if code in "01"` / `in "02"` pair of `pyte/streams.py`), so an
            `ESC ] 8 ; params ; URI ST` was consumed and DROPPED: measured through
            `TerminalScreen.feed` + `snapshot()`, the cell of a linked word had no hyperlink to
            answer with, and the canvas had nothing to make clickable.
            Why the CELL and not a map beside the grid: every write path already builds its cell
            from `self.cursor.attrs` (`draw()`'s `_replace(data=char)`), so a link held in the
            attributes is inherited by the characters written after it and travels WITH the cell
            through `draw()`, `erase_characters`, `erase_in_line`/`erase_in_display`, the insert
            family and the scroll. A parallel `{(row, col): uri}` map would be a second truth that
            pyte's own erase and scroll would not maintain, and the fork's policy is that the
            emulator is the ONE owner of the emulation (AGENTS.md §4.7).
            Two rules this patch DECLARES: (1) the `params` half (`id=…`) is ACCEPTED and IGNORED
            — an id only groups the cells of one link, while the URI is what a canvas opens; an
            EMPTY params half therefore makes the whole tail the URI, which is the OSC 8 reading.
            (2) SGR 0 is ORTHOGONAL to OSC 8: `select_graphic_rendition` rebuilds the attributes
            from `default_char` on BOTH of its paths, so both paths re-apply the current
            hyperlink; a link is closed by `ESC ] 8 ; ; ST` and by `Screen.reset()` (which
            rebuilds the attributes) and by nothing else.
Base:       pyte 0.8.2 (PyPI sdist, sha256 in MANIFEST.md), pyte/screens.py and pyte/streams.py
            (after patches 0001-0010; 0001-0005 and 0007-0009 touched screens.py, 0006 and 0010
            touched streams.py).
Policy:     keep until upstream implements OSC 8 — `0.8.3.dev` has no hyperlink support at all
            (its OSC branch is behaviourally unchanged), so this is a fork feature rather than a
            fix waiting for a release; the `Char` field is additive, so a future rebase can keep
            the canvas side and drop the patch at any time.
Applied:    2026-10-07, sshmap v1.9.

